      "message": "My understanding is that `is_wasm` will also be true when we specifically tell a target to be built via the wasm toolchain, i.e. via `(//build/toolchain/wasm:wasm)`. Previously, in the `samples` target, because we additionally specify to build the samples with the wasm, any dependencies that the samples need are rebuilt in a subdir where `is_wasm` is effectively true throughout the BUILD files used to generate the targets.\n\nThat said, I agree that this `is_wasm` probably wasn\u0027t doing much since this target was never built with the wasm toolchain anywhere. I think in particular it makes sense to use `dawn_wasm` in this `BUILD` file because we are essentially just trying to decide what defaults should be built when building all of Dawn. All that is to say that this LGTM!",
